#
# Semantic content of the header page: values, relations and properties.
# The presence of each name and type comes with the Tier 0 generator.

assertion  XBD.assert.h.001
anchor     basedefs/assert.h.html#DESCRIPTION/assert
class      required
since      1988
says       assert is a macro; when NDEBUG is not defined a true assertion has no
           effect and its expression is evaluated once; after NDEBUG is defined
           and <assert.h> included again the expression is not evaluated;
           undefining NDEBUG and including it once more makes assert evaluate it
           again.
test       t/001-assert-macro.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.assert.h.002
anchor     basedefs/assert.h.html#DESCRIPTION/assert
class      required
since      1988
says       A false assertion ends the process abnormally while NDEBUG is not
           defined, and does nothing after NDEBUG is defined and <assert.h> is
           included again.
note       What the abnormal end looks like (message, signal) is on the assert()
           page; here only that the process does not carry on normally.
test       t/002-assert-ndebug-state.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
